+ * An Android key code names a key, not the character on it. The key is known from the hardware
+ * key code (letters, digits and punctuation keep their code under any layout); the key value only
+ * decides for keys the table does not know. A key value that is no key (a Cyrillic letter, say)
+ * must not leak into the key code.
